+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus whose records drew from the same 30-word
+vocabulary, the measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` hook p95 was **10.27
+ms** before the term-selection fix. Common terms produced long FTS posting
+lists even though they carried little retrieval signal.
+
+The fix changed term selection to discard a term when its document frequency
+is greater than one third of the store (`df > n / 3`; applied to stores with at
+least 50 records). The synthetic benchmark vocabulary was also changed to a
+Zipf distribution: 30 frequent domain words plus 2,000 rare identifiers, so
+the post-fix measurement is not a controlled one-variable comparison.
+
+With those changes in place, the measured full-recall p95 was **1.82 ms**.
